#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""autobot - drive an automated DayZ client (and a throwaway test server) for mod testing.

Local commands:
  setup                     build @DayZAutobot (tools/build) and prepare the client prefix
  build                     pack DayZAutobot/ into build/@DayZAutobot
  launch [--connect HOST[:PORT]] [--mods a,b] [--name N] [--window WxH] [--display virtual|desktop] [--no-wait]
                            start the isolated client; waits for the main menu (or in game with --connect).
                            By default it runs in a headless KWin (invisible, own Xwayland, real GPU);
                            --display desktop shows the window (it grabs the mouse when focused)
  kill                      kill the client (its Proton prefix only; your own game is never touched)
  server-start [--mission DIR|TERRAIN] [--mods a,b] [--server-mods a,b] [--wipe] [--no-wait]
                            deploy a throwaway mission and start the stable server (port 2402, no BattlEye)
  server-stop               ask the server to exit, kill it if it doesn't
  join                      connect the client to the throwaway server and wait until in game
  cycle [--server]          rebuild, restart server + client with their last settings, rejoin
  ps                        what's running (client, server, bridge) and what has polled the bridge
  paths                     every location in use
  log [-n N] [--grep RE] [--server]   newest script log of the client (or server)
  bridge                    run the bridge in the foreground (normally started automatically)

Game commands (sent to the client; prefix with `server` to send to the test server instead):
  autobot status            autobot server status
  autobot help              lists every game command with usage
  autobot exec code='return GetGame().GetPlayer().GetType();'
  autobot screenshot [width=960] [hud=false]   -> PNG path (X11 grab of this instance's window)
  autobot enter [target=<vehicle id|type>] [seat=0]   walk to the seat's door, open it, get in
  autobot leave                                       get out (opening the door from inside if shut)

Arguments are key=value. Options: --instance NAME (default: default), --game stable|exp,
--raw (one-line JSON), --timeout SECS.
"""
